comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-24T08:52:02.601Z",pi-agent,"Round-3 CodeRabbit findings on PR 16, all resolved in source with revert-verified regression tests:\n\n- transfer.ts + gatesim.ts: locale-sensitive sorts feeding content-addressed hashes replaced with byte order (Buffer.compare) at three sites; pinned by gap/gate/episode byte-order tests that flip under a localeCompare revert.\n- receipt.ts: two raw library keys normalizing to one name now refuse with duplicate_receipt_library instead of silently overwriting the first version.\n- sweep.ts: MAX_SWEEP_ARMS (64) cap added to expandSearchSpace with the typed search_space_too_large refusal, plus one shared METRIC_NAME_PATTERN and an isSelectionRuleKind guard replacing duplicated regex/kind checks.\n- index.ts: rl run start now declares the optional --receipt-file flag its handler already read.\n- README.md: GateEpisode and MergeOutcome rows added so the What-it-tracks table lists all nine registered types.\n- test/sweep.test.ts: parseSweepSpec refusals now assert typed codes; the before-anything-is-written plan test asserts neither sweep nor arm exists after each refusal.\n- transfer.ts: per_metric docstring now states the Number.NaN hole and its null JSON serialization.\n\nRevert-proof verification: each behavioural fix was temporarily reverted via git stash and its pinned test confirmed FAILING (receipt duplicate: 1 fail; arm cap: 2 fails across unit and plan tests; transfer byte sort: 1 fail; gatesim byte sorts: 2 fails; receipt-file flag: 1 fail), then restored."
  "2026-08-24T09:31:02.941Z",pi-agent,"Round-3b follow-up: the two feature-record projections now carry the provenance citations as linked file evidence (.agents/pm/features/pm-rl-06n6.toon and .agents/pm/features/pm-rl-0cqg.toon, each holding a comment that cites its exact regression-test titles), and the dpug history stream holds the appended corrective provenance entry (./node_modules/.bin/pm, version 2026.8.20). Exact test titles cited per record are listed in this task's earlier comment."
